        "html": "<article style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:30px;border-radius:28px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#020617,#1e1b4b,#134e4a);color:white;font-family:system-ui'><small style='letter-spacing:.18em;color:#67e8f9'>AI ARCHITECTURE MAP</small><h1 style='font:850 38px Georgia;margin:18px 0 10px'>Eight Ways AI Models Are Built to Think and Work</h1><p style='font-size:17px;color:#dbeafe;max-width:650px'>The model changes with the job: language, vision, context, concepts, action, routing, or pixel-level segmentation.</p><div style='font-size:30px;margin-top:30px;color:#a5f3fc'>read · see · understand · plan · act</div></article>",
