      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# 🧭 Architecture Follows Function\n\nA chatbot, an image generator, and an agent that books a flight may belong to the same AI ecosystem, but they do not necessarily use the same architecture.\n\nThe central idea of the post is simple: **different model designs specialize in different kinds of input, reasoning, and output.**",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "eight-ai-model-architectures"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786024515001,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
