        "status": "available",
        "capturedAt": "2026-08-06T14:05:00.000Z",
        "summary": "This conversation transformed a social-media post about eight AI model categories into a structured Twilite explainer graph.\n\nIt created dedicated nodes for LLM, SLM, VLM, MLM, LCM, LAM, MoE, and SAM, connected them through the idea that architecture follows function, and brought them together in a convergence node describing multimodal AI systems.\n\nThe graph also added a taxonomy note explaining that the labels describe different dimensions rather than one perfectly uniform classification system. The visual palette was then darkened for a richer presentation.",
        "excerpt": "Make a graph about this post: Most of you are aware of LLMs, but there are eight types of AI models.",
        "notes": "Owner-only provenance record for the conversation that created and revised this graph. No shared discussion URL has been stored.",
